            <ArticleTitle>Sciatica leading to the discovery of a renal cell carcinoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>18</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Metastatic renal cell cancer is not exceptional in kidney cancer (30% of patients with kidneyl cancer). Its prognosis is particularly severe. However, sciatic neuralgia (sciatica) remains an exceptional revealing clinical sign of this disease. The authors report the case of a patient admitted with right sciatica as chief complain, leading to the discovery of a renal cell carcinoma. Although uncommon, renal cell carcinoma spine metastasis should be included in the differential diagnosis of back pain and sciatica.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
